    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The colonization of Canada in the mid 1800's involved mass mistreatment of First Nations previously occupying the land. This mistreatment was perpetuated for centuries, with inhumane acts such as mandatory Residential schools. While there have been measures taken by both the Canadian Government and local communities to try to make up for past wrong-doings, there is still a great urgency for action to be taken to solve the social, political, financial and environmental issues facing theses communities, and to reconcile these cultures.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
